    "problem": "Which of the following data sets **might** be normally distributed?",
    "worked_solution": "If a large data set is normally distributed, it should be approximately bell-shaped. \n\nAmong the given options, the only bell-shaped curve is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070457/assets/925a72e15da6d9ace52507e88a92da4a4e82d17b073fe6d6bcb4d6c14f716da4.png)\n\nIt's important to note that other bell-shaped distributions exist. Therefore, further tests on the data are required to confirm whether the underlying distribution is normal.",
